KG42.register("rules-bd1b576d0282b1a384b20324",{"id":"12-p2p_microgrid_trading::v141-c-R001","paper":"12-p2p_microgrid_trading","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R001","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Energy-trade execution","process_stage":"activation","market_meaning":"Peers buy or sell energy directly with each other without conventional energy suppliers acting as intermediaries. Scope: Direct P2P energy purchases and sales between peers. A prosumer with surplus electricity may sell it to other energy consumers. Scope: Sale of surplus electricity by prosumers to other energy consumers. Condition: The prosumer has surplus electricity. A Microgrid, a Cell or a region may be considered a peer and trade with other such peers. Scope: P2P architecture at Microgrid, Cell and region scales.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function execution.energy_trade under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["execution.energy_trade"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"Direct P2P energy purchases and sales between peers. | P2P architecture at Microgrid, Cell and region scales. | Sale of surplus electricity by prosumers to other energy consumers.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02","v141-b-g01-ev-03","v141-b-g01-ev-09"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Peers buy or sell energy directly with each other without conventional energy suppliers acting as intermediaries. Scope: Direct P2P energy purchases and sales between peers.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-02"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A prosumer with surplus electricity may sell it to other energy consumers. Scope: Sale of surplus electricity by prosumers to other energy consumers. Condition: The prosumer has surplus electricity.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-03"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A Microgrid, a Cell or a region may be considered a peer and trade with other such peers. Scope: P2P architecture at Microgrid, Cell and region scales.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-09"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-02","location":{"location_id":"src-c1934be9b4-p01-c1r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"1. Introduction","anchor_text":"system. go A peer in the P2P energy trading refers to one or a group of local ti energy customers, i","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A peer in the P2P energy trading refers to one or a group of local energy customers, including generators, consumers and prosumers. The peers buy or sell energy directly with each other without intermediation by conventional energy suppliers [3]. P2P energy trading is usually enabled by Information and Communication Technologies (ICT) -based online services [2]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-03","location":{"location_id":"src-c1934be9b4-p01-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"1. Introduction","anchor_text":"Bidding system ments and technologies involved i Game theory energy trading was simulated usin Deman","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"With the increasing connection of Distributed Energy Resources (DERs), traditional energy consumers are becoming prosumers, who can both consume and generate energy [1]. Electricity generation of DERs is usually intermittent and difficult to predict. When prosumers have surplus electricity, they can curtail it, store it with energy storage devices, export it back to the power grid, or sell it to other energy consumers. The direct energy trading among consumers and prosumers is called Peer-to-Peer (P2P) energy trading, which is developed based on the “P2P economy” concept (also known as sharing economy) [2], and is usually implemented within a local electricity distribution system."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-09","location":{"location_id":"src-c1934be9b4-p03-c1r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. Four-layer system architecture of Peer-to-Peer energy trading","anchor_text":"g , p coordinated way either connected to the main power network or is- ti landed. A Microgrid norma","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 1","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Individual premise refers to one single house connected to the electricity distribution system. Microgrids are electricity distribution systems containing loads and DERs, which operate in a controlled and coordinated way either connected to the main power network or islanded. A Microgrid normally consists of a collection of individual premises and DERs in a local geographical area that share the same medium-voltage/low-voltage (MV/LV) transformer. Similarly, Cell is a concept proposed in studies [18,19], and is an entity that consists of a number of Microgrids. It is used to define a wider area of network in which a collection of DERs can be controlled in response to a number of objectives [20]. A Cell may contain several Microgrids, and may also operate in either grid-connected or islanded mode. A region can be as large as a city or a metropolitan area which consists of multiple Cells. A Microgrid, a Cell or a region can all be considered as a peer and trade with each other."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"The evidence for this rule is definitional/procedural prose about peer participation and direct trading; it introduces no optimization or design variables. The paper's quantitative variables (e.g. Eout-i-k, uk, σ, βi) appear only in the bidding-game mechanism v141-a-M03 and are not declared in this rule's frozen graph. No source-supported variable for execution.energy_trade is present in the supplied evidence.","empty_theta_reason":"No parameters are stated in the supplied evidence for this rule. Constants such as L and ε appear in the payoff function of v141-a-M03, not in the evidence frozen for v141-c-R001. The rule's evidence contains no numeric, symbolic or bounded coefficients to record as parameters."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-02","quote":"The peers buy or sell energy directly with each other without intermediation by conventional energy suppliers [3]."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-03","quote":"When prosumers have surplus electricity, they can curtail it, store it with energy storage devices, export it back to the power grid, or sell it to other energy consumers."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-09","quote":"A Microgrid, a Cell or a region can all be considered as a peer and trade with each other."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"a1f944fa20435edda9c35ce9eca6d50d7dc6cd404e156ea86360bc7bdf236e5e","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule v141-c-R001 contains only definitional/procedural statements about who may trade energy directly under the activation-stage function execution.energy_trade. The supplied evidence texts (v141-b-g01-ev-02, v141-b-g01-ev-03, v141-b-g01-ev-09) are prose definitions of peer participation, surplus sale and peer aggregation; they contain no equations, variables, parameters, quantifiers over quantitative objects, or optimization constraints for this rule. The paper's mathematical content (payoff function, Nash equilibrium, water-temperature dynamics) belongs to distinct mechanisms/rules (e.g. v141-a-M03, v141-a-M04) and is not part of the evidence frozen for this rule. Therefore no mathematical formalization is supported for this activation-stage rule. Per the experimental source-review policy, B evidence is unreviewed; this classification uses the supplied quotations as provisional support but does not assert independent verification.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","node_ids":["execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C001 is a procedural scope statement about direct peer-to-peer energy trading without conventional supplier intermediation. It constrains the activation-stage function node execution.energy_trade; the frozen graph E contains no edge for this unary relation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-C002","node_ids":["execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 is a conditional procedural statement about a prosumer with surplus electricity selling to other energy consumers. It constrains the activation-stage function node execution.energy_trade; no frozen edge represents this unary relation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-C003","node_ids":["execution.energy_trade"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C003 is a scope statement that Microgrids, Cells or regions may act as peers and trade with each other. It maps to the activation-stage function node execution.energy_trade; the frozen graph has no edge for this unary relation."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
